package httpapi

/*
What each route is for.

Generated once from the routing table and kept beside it, so the description
this server publishes is a description of what it serves. The summaries come
from the handlers' own names rather than from prose somebody wrote separately:
a name is what the code already agrees on, and it cannot drift from the thing
it names.

A route with no entry here is reported by Undocumented, and a test fails on
that. Adding a route therefore means saying what it is for — which is a small
tax at the moment somebody knows the answer, rather than an archaeology problem
for whoever needs the description later.
*/
